WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.779
Pycelle: Without question, Oldtown is the
oldest, wealthiest, and greatest city in Westeros.

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:12.290
Qyburn: Though King's Landing is more populous,
and arguably, more powerful.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.200
Pycelle: The city straddles the mouth of the
Honeywine River, and the bounty of the entire

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.280
Reach flows beneath its stone bridges to ports
that are renowned throughout the world.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.802
Qyburn: Thus, we needn't speak more of them.

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:29.930
More interesting is the history of the city,
for none can say when it was founded.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:35.070
Many centuries ago, a few bold maesters sought
out the Children of the Forest, who claimed

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.170
that men have lived at the mouth of the Honeywine
since the Dawn Age.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.790
Pycelle: Nonsense.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:46.160
Maester Jellicoe proved that the city began
as a trading post where ships from Valyria,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.080
Old Ghis, and the Summer Isles put in to replenish
their provisions and make repairs.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:57.520
Hence, the most famous feature of the city,
the Hightower, raised even before the city

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.100
walls as a beacon through the fog-covered
waters.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.870
Originally built of wood and standing a mere
fifty feet above the ancient fortress of its

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:13.450
foundation, it is now thick stone and rises
even taller than the Wall.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:18.000
Those born and raised in Oldtown can tell
the time of day by where its shadow falls.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.689
Qyburn: But no maester can tell why.

00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:26.869
Even in our oldest records, the island on
which it stands is called Battle Isle.

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:28.960
What battle was fought there?

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.000
And when?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.270
As for the ancient fortress that forms the
tower's base, its walls and interiors are

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.660
all of solid black stone with no hints of
joints.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.760
Or mortar.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.360
And no chisel marks of any kind.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.700
We know it predates the tower itself by thousands
of years.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.140
But who built it?

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.140
How?

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.410
And against what?

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:56.660
Pycelle: The maesters who have studied it
declare it to be of Valyrian construction,

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.369
akin to Dragonstone and the Black Walls of
Volantis.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:05.790
As is well-known, the dragonlords of Valyria
could turn stone to liquid with dragonflame

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.980
to shape it as they wished.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:12.379
Qyburn: Didn't one Archmaester link the fortress
to the vanished mazemakers of Lorath?

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:18.180
And another maester to the legendary Deep
Ones who inhabited the Iron Islands before

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.790
the Ironborn?

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.890
Pycelle: Both marginal opinions without common
support.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:30.220
But of more importance than the origin of
the tower is the family to which it gave its

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.220
name.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:37.540
House Hightower.The ancient ruling family
of Oldtown.Known for their prudence and love

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:38.540
of peace.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.400
Qyburn: And pieces of gold.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.470
Pycelle: During the Age of Heroes, when Lymond
Hightower saw the Gardener kings conquering

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:50.529
the Reach, he didn't beat them on the battlefield,
but in the godswood.

00:02:50.529 --> 00:02:53.430
He bound his house to theirs by marriage.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:59.309
And transformed House Hightower from wealthy
but relatively minor kings to the greatest

00:02:59.309 --> 00:03:01.420
lords of the Reach.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:07.250
Thanks to Lord Lymond's foresight, Highgarden
has always defended Oldtown, allowing the

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:11.549
Hightowers to focus on higher pursuits such
as learning and trade.

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:14.330
Qyburn: On that, we agree.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:20.379
When the Andals invaded Westeros, Lord Dorian
Hightower told his wife of twenty years that

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:27.010
wars are bad for trade, and, to make his point,
traded her for a young Andal princess.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:33.220
When Aegon the Conqueror was earning his name,
House Hightower traded its loyalty to the

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:41.450
Gardeners for his confirmation of their rights,
welcoming him with open arms and open gates.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:47.279
Pycelle: House Hightower bent the knee to
Aegon to spare the city from his dragons.

00:03:47.279 --> 00:03:52.219
I would think such insinuations and insults
beneath even you, Qyburn.

00:03:52.219 --> 00:03:56.609
Then again, mockery of one's betters is the
trade of fools.

00:03:56.609 --> 00:03:59.349
Qyburn: I wouldn't know.

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:02.569
Perhaps if I'd studied at the Citadel as long
as you, Grand Maester.

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:07.370
Pycelle: The Citadel is the greatest seat
of learning in the known world.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:12.510
Without it, and the maesters it trains, Westeros
would be a land of superstition and ignorance.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:17.139
Qyburn: Like the ignorance that shrouds the
Citadel's own birth?

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:21.901
Pycelle: Even without records, we have more
than enough reason to believe that the Citadel

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:28.909
began as a court of scholars and priests assembled
by a second son of House Hightower.

00:04:28.909 --> 00:04:33.789
When he died, his elder brother raised the
Citadel so that wise men would always have

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:39.169
a home in Westeros and could continue the
inquiries and debates that had given such

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:40.820
joy to his younger brother.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.770
Qyburn: His little brother's pets, as legend
has it, he called them.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:48.090
And so the maesters have remained.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.870
Only their masters have changed.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:57.960
Now they serve every lord with a castle for
a fee, of course, whilst the Citadel serves

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.949
its own importance.

00:05:00.949 --> 00:05:07.300
Pycelle: Every word you speak merely validates
your own expulsion from our ranks.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.960
Qyburn: Knowledge is validation enough.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.590
I assume the world's greatest minds would
agree.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.430
And perhaps they would if I'd met them.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.380
Oldtown is a city for old men and old beliefs.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.790
Samwell Tarly: The Citadel of Oldtown is the
greatest center of learning in the world,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:27.669
not that it has much competition, really.

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:32.380
Most lords think of books the way they think
of younger sons, useful to have around as

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.090
long as they keep to the corners.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:40.659
Back when House Hightower still ruled Oldtown
as kings, a crippled younger son sought solace

00:05:40.659 --> 00:05:45.960
in books and those who wrote them and became
the greatest patron of learning in his day.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.720
Scholars of all sorts flocked to Oldtown to
debate and write and.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.189
debate.

00:05:52.189 --> 00:05:56.949
After this Prince Peremore's death, his brother
granted land to "Peremore's Pets," as the

00:05:56.949 --> 00:06:00.669
wise men were called, though now they're known
as maesters.

00:06:00.669 --> 00:06:06.530
Viserys Targaryen:The Dance began, as many
dances do, with an old man and a young girl.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:11.110
The queen had failed to produce a son for
her king, so he anointed his daughter, the

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.680
Princess Rhaenyra, as his heir.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.650
But years later, the king remarried, and his
new wife, Queen Alicent of House Hightower,

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.889
gave him a son.

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:22.759
Feeble and foolish, the old king refused to
change the succession.

00:06:22.759 --> 00:06:27.889
He didn't even see how his court had split
into two rival camps of Blacks and Greens,

00:06:27.889 --> 00:06:34.979
after the dresses that the princess and the
queen had worn to some tourney.

00:06:34.979 --> 00:06:39.400
One night, a servant found the old king had
died in his sleep and ran to inform Queen

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.259
Alicent.

00:06:41.259 --> 00:06:45.219
Protocol dictated that the bells would be
rung and a ravensent to Dragonstone to summon

00:06:45.219 --> 00:06:48.540
the heir, Princess Rhaenyra, for her coronation.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.569
But Alicent had other plans.

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:55.749
Once she saw her dead husband's body, she
sealed the room and had the servant thrown

00:06:55.749 --> 00:06:58.539
into the Black Cells to ensure his silence.

00:06:58.539 --> 00:07:03.319
At the hour of the owl, the Lord Commander
of the Kingsguard, Ser Criston Cole, summoned

00:07:03.319 --> 00:07:06.169
the small council to inform them of the king's
death.

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:10.759
Ser Otto Hightower, the Hand of the King and
father to Queen Alicent, demanded that the

00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:12.229
succession be settled immediately.

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:18.530
The decrepit old men of the small council
were confused; the succession was settled

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.639
in their minds.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:24.819
The old king had forced the lords of Westeros
to swear fealty to Princess Rhaenyra as his

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:25.819
heir.

00:07:25.819 --> 00:07:30.849
But Ser Criston Cole rightly pointed out that
a son comes before a daughter.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:36.210
The council argued until dawn when the Master
of Coin finally stood up and declared he would

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.689
have no part of treason.

00:07:37.689 --> 00:07:43.590
Ser Criston Cole wisely opened his throat
with a dagger, ending the debate.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:47.550
None were more surprised to hear of Prince
Aegon's succession than Prince Aegon himself.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:52.559
At first, the fool rejected the crown, but
his mother pointed out that his sister Rhaenyra

00:07:52.559 --> 00:07:55.389
would return such loyalty by taking his head.

00:07:55.389 --> 00:07:59.150
As the old king's trueborn son, he'd always
be a threat.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.389
Aegon relented.

00:08:00.389 --> 00:08:04.439
He was crowned in the Dragonpit, and his wife
and sister Helaena became queen.

00:08:04.439 --> 00:08:08.639
His brother Aemondflew off to win over the
few great lords whose support Aegon didn't

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:09.639
already have.

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:14.931
The banner of the gold dragon flew over King's
Landing and the Red Keep as Aegon, Second

00:08:14.931 --> 00:08:17.199
of His Name, ascended the Iron Throne.

00:08:17.199 --> 00:08:22.699
Catelyn Stark: When Rhaenyra heard of her
son's death, she collapsed.

00:08:22.699 --> 00:08:28.749
She considered ending the war right then until
a raven arrived from her husband, Daemon.

00:08:28.749 --> 00:08:32.709
Her son would be avenged.

00:08:32.709 --> 00:08:36.760
Whispers slithered through the taverns and
back alleys of Flea Bottom.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:43.789
Two men were found; one was a former gold
cloak, the other a rat catcher in the Red

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.940
Keep who knew all its secrets.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:51.589
History remembers them only as Blood and Cheese.

00:08:51.589 --> 00:08:55.990
One night, Queen Helaena entered the royal
apartments with her daughter and two sons

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:57.890
to put them to bed.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:02.100
Without warning, Blood and Cheese burst in,
daggers in hand.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.380
They told her that a debt was owed.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.830
A son for a son.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:11.620
Blood and Cheese demanded she choose which
son would be ripped from her forever.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:16.570
Queen Helaena pleaded with the men to kill
her instead, but they refused.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:21.490
Weeping, Helaena named her younger son Maelor.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:26.829
Perhaps she thought the boy was too young
to understand, perhaps because the older boy

00:09:26.829 --> 00:09:30.770
was King Aegon's firstborn son and heir.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.060
"You hear that, little boy?"

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.570
Cheese whispered to the younger son.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:39.029
"Your mama wants you dead."

00:09:39.029 --> 00:09:43.220
Then Blood struck off the older boy's head
with a single blow.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:48.370
When the guards burst in, they found Queen
Helaena still screaming, clasping her dead

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:52.020
son's body to her, mad with grief.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:57.040
The blood of her children transformed a dynastic
dispute into a war of annihilation.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:03.670
The grief and rage of losing a child could
burn down the world.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:08.060
Either Aegon or Rhaenyra could live at the
end, but not both.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:13.600
Robert Baratheon: One day King's Landing looked
up and saw two dragons circling their foul

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:14.600
city.

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:21.040
Daemon and Rhaenyra had come for her throne,
for the city was defenseless.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:27.779
Aemond had taken the king's army from the
city, and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar.

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:33.190
Seeing that resistance was hopeless, the small
council surrendered the city, the Queen Mother

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:37.120
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.889
But not King Aegon.

00:10:38.889 --> 00:10:48.860
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,
he had vanished from the city.

